# coding: latin-1
"""Isolated probe (Passo 1, esperimento binario/tinier -- see
crypto_collateral_risk_binary_produzione_sperimentale.mpc): verifies
that secret comparisons in the binary domain can be combined with
NATIVE bitwise operators (&, |, ^, ~) instead of arithmetic (+, -, *)
on already-revealed flags, and that .reveal() on the composed result is
correct -- as opposed to the ALREADY-known-broken case (see
crypto_collateral_risk.mpc's compute_flags docstring) of | / & on
regint/cint values obtained by revealing binary-domain secrets
individually first. Here the flags stay SECRET (sbitintvec, 1 bit wide
-- comparison operators' own comp_result) until the composed boolean
is revealed once.

Three known input pairs, hardcoded as public ints then converted to
sint (still exercises real secret comparison circuits, not a
compile-time constant fold -- sint(int) with a compile-time-known value
still emits real MPC instructions, same pattern credit_score.mpc /
crypto_collateral_risk.mpc use throughout for their own sint(...)
comparisons against policy constants).

Pair 1: a=5,  b=10  -> a<b True,  a>b False, a==b False
Pair 2: a=10, b=5   -> a<b False, a>b True,  a==b False
Pair 3: a=7,  b=7   -> a<b False, a>b False, a==b True

For each pair, prints: lt, gt, eq (each a plain reveal(), sanity
baseline) then and_lt_gt (lt & gt, expect always 0), or_lt_gt (lt | gt,
expect 1 iff a!=b), xor_lt_gt (lt ^ gt, expect same as or here since
lt/gt are mutually exclusive), not_lt (~lt, expect the boolean
negation of lt, i.e. 1-lt).
"""

pairs = [(5, 10), (10, 5), (7, 7)]

for idx, (a_val, b_val) in enumerate(pairs):
    a = sint(a_val)
    b = sint(b_val)

    lt = (a < b)
    gt = (a > b)
    eq = (a == b)

    and_lt_gt = lt & gt
    or_lt_gt = lt | gt
    xor_lt_gt = lt ^ gt
    not_lt = ~lt

    print_ln('--- pair %s: a=%s b=%s ---', idx, a_val, b_val)
    print_ln('lt: %s', lt.reveal())
    print_ln('gt: %s', gt.reveal())
    print_ln('eq: %s', eq.reveal())
    print_ln('and_lt_gt: %s', and_lt_gt.reveal())
    print_ln('or_lt_gt: %s', or_lt_gt.reveal())
    print_ln('xor_lt_gt: %s', xor_lt_gt.reveal())
    print_ln('not_lt: %s', not_lt.reveal())
